WEBVTT

00:00:02.799 --> 00:00:08.750
<v Callum Reid>Morning, everyone. Monday the thirteenth. Can you hear me all right? Teams reckons my microphone's somewhere else.</v>

00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:15.070
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, you're coming through. Unlike the broken coffee machine in the canteen. Absolutely nothing coming through that.</v>

00:00:16.019 --> 00:00:19.170
<v Jamie Brennan>Probably doing us a favour, judging by Friday's coffee.</v>

00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:25.559
<v Marcus Hale>Needed something after the football last night. Sat through all that and then couldn't get to sleep.</v>

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:29.760
<v David Whitfield>You could've watched it again. That would've done it.</v>

00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:35.950
<v Callum Reid>Right, before this becomes the sports desk. Fiona, what's already off the list?</v>

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:43.280
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah so, already swapped the filter on the CT1 yesterday. That's finished, not something to allocate again.</v>

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.979
<v Callum Reid>Good, CT1 closed.</v>

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.700
<v Marcus Hale>And I already swapped the filter on the HV board yesterday. That's done as well.</v>

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:57.750
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, you clipped out after filter. HV board, did you say?</v>

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.600
<v Marcus Hale>HV board, yeah. Yesterday. Finished.</v>

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:10.000
<v Fiona Doyle>The other carry-over is still waiting on parts for the PRV on the boiler. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.870
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, no change on the parts position. Still not here.</v>

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:21.140
<v Callum Reid>So that stays blocked. No boiler PRV work being handed out this morning.</v>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.900
<v Grace Liu>Understood. Blocked means blocked, not squeeze it in somehow.</v>

00:01:26.739 --> 00:01:32.689
<v Callum Reid>Grace Liu, can you replace the seals on the Water Booster Pump? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:01:34.069 --> 00:01:38.969
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll replace the seals on the Water Booster Pump. Understood on the priority.</v>

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:43.079
<v David Whitfield>Just the seals, we're saying? Not a whole pump replacement?</v>

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:49.459
<v Callum Reid>Just replace the seals on the Water Booster Pump, yes. That's the scope.</v>

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.480
<v Grace Liu>Fine. I've got that one, and it's ahead of the routine stuff.</v>

00:01:56.659 --> 00:02:00.510
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, that's clear. Not putting that down as a normal-priority job.</v>

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:09.830
<v Callum Reid>And Grace, can you go to Northfield Substation to pick up the replacement parts for the IM2 today at 2pm? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:02:10.719 --> 00:02:15.620
<v Grace Liu>Today at 2pm, at Northfield Substation? Just making sure I've heard the time properly.</v>

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.090
<v Callum Reid>Yes, today at 2pm. That pickup is also a drop-everything one.</v>

00:02:22.729 --> 00:02:29.030
<v Grace Liu>Okay, I'll go to Northfield Substation to pick up the replacement parts for the IM2 today at 2pm.</v>

00:02:30.219 --> 00:02:36.169
<v Jamie Brennan>That's collection only, isn't it? Not collecting and then fitting them as part of the same thing?</v>

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:41.009
<v Grace Liu>Collection only, yeah. I'm accepting the pickup, not an IM2 installation job.</v>

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:49.680
<v Fiona Doyle>So two top-priority items with Grace. One's got the fixed 2pm time; the seals haven't got a separate deadline stated.</v>

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.780
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. Both urgent, and I'm not adding another time onto the seals.</v>

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:04.789
<v Marcus Hale>While we're on equipment, I heard a slight rattle from the Air Compressor 1. Nothing to action yet, just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.169
<v Hannah Price>Right, an observation, rather than another job?</v>

00:03:10.069 --> 00:03:12.169
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, exactly. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:21.210
<v Jamie Brennan>Similar sort of note from me: noticed the IM2 was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.500
<v Hannah Price>It did settle, then? Wasn't still climbing?</v>

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:33.689
<v Jamie Brennan>No, it settled down. That's just the nights observation, not me asking for more work on it.</v>

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.990
<v Callum Reid>Okay. Neither of those becomes a new action off the back of this call.</v>

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:47.849
<v Jamie Brennan>Um, separately, I'll swap the filter on the compressor one tomorrow morning. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:48.509 --> 00:03:51.310
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomorrow morning for that filter, rather than today?</v>

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:59.569
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, tomorrow morning. I'll take it. It matters but it's not urgent, so no drop-everything treatment on that.</v>

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:06.469
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, Jamie. The filter on the compressor one is yours for tomorrow morning, at that priority.</v>

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:12.849
<v David Whitfield>And we're not quietly turning that into a rattle investigation as well?</v>

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:19.250
<v Jamie Brennan>No, just the filter swap I've volunteered for. Separate from Marcus's observation.</v>

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:24.269
<v Marcus Hale>Lovely. Otherwise one sentence from me turns into a strip-down.</v>

00:04:24.829 --> 00:04:32.879
<v Callum Reid>For the line 1 TCU, I'll run a function test on Friday. That's an 'if you've got a spare minute' one, low priority.</v>

00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:37.750
<v Hannah Price>Function test only, yeah? Not changing settings as part of it?</v>

00:04:38.899 --> 00:04:43.800
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll run a function test on the line 1 TCU, nothing beyond that.</v>

00:04:45.709 --> 00:04:50.259
<v Fiona Doyle>Callum Reid on that one, on Friday, low priority — the spare-minute job.</v>

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.980
<v Callum Reid>That's me, yes. On Friday.</v>

00:04:56.199 --> 00:05:04.250
<v Fiona Doyle>There's still the need to schedule downtime for the line 2 interlock with production next Tuesday. Normal priority. It hasn't got an owner.</v>

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.180
<v Callum Reid>Anyone able to take ownership of scheduling that with production?</v>

00:05:10.579 --> 00:05:14.779
<v Fiona Doyle>I can't take ownership of it. I'm raising the gap, not volunteering.</v>

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:17.410
<v David Whitfield>Can't take that one either, sorry.</v>

00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:22.069
<v Grace Liu>Not me on top of the two we've just agreed.</v>

00:05:24.079 --> 00:05:31.430
<v Callum Reid>All right, nobody's taken it. Schedule downtime for the line 2 interlock with production next Tuesday, normal priority — still unowned.</v>

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:37.629
<v Hannah Price>So it's not sitting against Fiona just because she read it out?</v>

00:05:39.889 --> 00:05:43.740
<v Callum Reid>Correct. No owner. Don't want that getting mistaken for an acceptance.</v>

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.199
<v Marcus Hale>Same principle applies to me mentioning the coffee machine, by the way.</v>

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.459
<v Jamie Brennan>Don't worry, nobody mistook that for you volunteering.</v>

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:56.959
<v Callum Reid>Right. Anything we've accidentally doubled up before we finish?</v>

00:05:59.149 --> 00:06:05.800
<v Fiona Doyle>No. CT1 and HV board filters are already finished. PRV on the boiler is still blocked, not today's work.</v>

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.529
<v Marcus Hale>And my rattle was just information. No extra job from me.</v>

00:06:12.829 --> 00:06:20.879
<v Grace Liu>I'm clear: Water Booster Pump seals, drop everything; and the IM2 replacement-parts pickup at Northfield Substation today at 2pm, same urgency. Both accepted.</v>

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:23.319
<v Jamie Brennan>All clear from me as well.</v>

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.850
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, everyone. That's us. Bye.</v>
